From fcb2cf86a57809d229b5b38d1c8bae04e0179064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:31:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] nemotron: one GPU's checkpoint prompt down kernels sum
 the expert width shares into bf16

On one GPU a prompt down block (tf_ck4_down_sum_prompt) takes a first-share plan item and runs each pair's shares in
turn (pair + s on expert s * experts + e), adds the alpha-scaled sums in share order and rounds to bf16 as
tf_super_combine rounds the share sum. The combine and the shared add then read one bf16 row a pick
(tf_super_combine_sums, tf_super_moe_out_sums) instead of two fp32 rows, with the same fma and add order; the routed
and the shared expert rows both come from it (cuda_latent_ck.summed). Decode passes, which may run the shared expert
on the side stream, and tensor-parallel ranks keep fp32 shares. `tf-cuda-test checkpoint` checks the combine and the
shared add over the sums against decode's fp32 shares at Super's routed (1,408 picks, 8 experts) and shared-expert
shapes.
